# Patches applied on every platform, before series.<platform>, to the one
# shared n9.0.2 source pin. Promote a per-platform patch here once another
# platform needs the same pool file, instead of copying it into another series.
# The pool entry stays the single source of truth and common patches apply first.
#
# The libdovi profile 7 to 8.1 conversion helper the MediaCodec and the
# VideoToolbox paths both call. It only builds where one of them is enabled,
# so elsewhere it costs one configure entry. First, so its Makefile lines land
# on the pristine file before any later patch reads them.
0021-dolby-vision-convert-profile7-rpu-to-p81.patch
0022-pgssub-clear-palette-clut-on-epoch-flush.patch
0023-http-chunked-end-is-not-a-premature-eof.patch
0029-tcp-resolve-each-address-family-separately.patch
# The HEVC decoder's Dolby Vision log noise, and its software-only tables,
# which no hwaccel reads (d3d11va, nvdec, vaapi and vulkan included).
0010-hevc-downlevel-duplicate-dovi-rpu-log.patch
0030-hevc-skip-software-tables-under-hwaccel.patch
# OpenSSL is the TLS backend on apple, android and windows. Linux configures
# GnuTLS, so tls_openssl.c is not compiled there and this changes nothing.
0035-tls-openssl-read-ahead.patch
# CVE-2026-107676 (HDR10+), 107677 (DASH), 107678 (MOV PSSH), and 107696 (RTSP).
# Backports are from FFmpeg upstream; the HDR10+ regression test is included.
0040-hdr-dynamic-metadata-saturation.patch
0041-hdr-dynamic-metadata-regression-test.patch
0042-avstring-empty-search-string.patch
0043-dash-byte-range-eof.patch
0044-encryption-info-iterative-free.patch
0045-encryption-info-append-side-data.patch
0046-mov-append-pssh-init-info.patch
0047-rtsp-limit-redirects.patch
